export default {"id":"bassstation-level-16","number":16,"title":"AFX Mode & Per-Key Patch Overlays","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"- Understand the technical architecture of AFX Mode, developed in collaboration with Richard D. James (Aphex Twin). - Master the 8-bank geometry, mapping 25 discrete patch parameter overlays across the two-octave physical keybed (C2–C4 at O","modules":[{"id":"bassstation-m-16-1","code":"16","title":"AFX Mode & Per-Key Patch Overlays","blurb":"- Understand the technical architecture of AFX Mode, developed in collaboration with Richard D. James (Aphex Twin). - Master the 8-bank geometry, mapping 25 discrete patch parameter overlays across the two-octave physical keybed (C2–C4 at O","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"bassstation-l-o-16","title":"Section overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Section 16.1 — AFX Mode Architecture, Overlay Programming & Components Management","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Section Learning Outcomes","level":3},{"type":"list","items":["Understand the technical architecture of <strong>AFX Mode</strong>, developed in collaboration with Richard D. James (Aphex Twin).","Master the 8-bank geometry, mapping 25 discrete patch parameter overlays across the two-octave physical keybed (C2–C4 at Octave 0).","Select overlay banks (<code>o-0</code> to <code>o-8</code>), edit per-key patches in real time, and commit bank writes to non-volatile memory.","Execute hardware <strong>Copy and Paste</strong> routines across key overlays (<code>CPY</code> / <code>PST</code>).","Enable overlay-specific <strong>Write Protection</strong> (<code>r-0</code> / <code>r-1</code>).","Delineate the parameter classes included in patch overlays versus global/arpeggiator exclusions.","Deploy Novation Components for AFX bank backup, Live Edit parameter management, and <strong>Autostep</strong> automated sampling."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-1","title":"16.1.1: The AFX Mode Paradigm","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"AFX Mode transforms the Bass Station II from a standard single-timbre monophonic synthesizer into an ultra-fast, dynamic multi-sound performance surface and analogue drum workstation."},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      AFX MODE LAYERED ARCHITECTURE\n   [Base Synthesizer Patch] (e.g., Sub Bass on Patch 10)\n              │\n              ▼ (Overlaid in Real Time by Active Overlay Bank)\n   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │ 25-Key Keybed (C2 to C4) ──► Each Key Holds a Custom Patch  │\n   ├───────────┬───────────┬───────────┬───────────┬─────────────┤\n   │ Key C2    │ Key C#2   │ Key D2    │ Key D#2   │ Key E2...   │\n   │ (Kick)    │ (Snare)   │ (ClosedHat│ (OpenHat) │ (Acid Zap)  │\n   │ • Osc FM  │ • Noise   │ • HP Filt │ • HP Filt │ • Diode Res │\n   │ • Fast Env│ • Snappy  │ • Short D │ • Long D  │ • Hard Drive│\n   └───────────┴───────────┴───────────┴───────────┴─────────────┘</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Overlay Mechanics</strong>:","Rather than storing completely separate patches, AFX Mode applies <strong>parameter delta overlays</strong> on top of the currently active base patch.","When a specific key is struck, the synthesizer instantly reprograms its internal analogue control registers within microseconds, allowing adjacent keys to produce vastly different sounds (e.g., an analog kick drum on C2, a white noise snare on D2, a closed hat on F#2, an FM metallic zap on G2, and a reese bass lead on C3)."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-2","title":"16.1.2: Bank Geometry (8 Banks × 25 Keys)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"The AFX Mode memory structure comprises:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>8 Total Overlay Banks</strong> (<code>o-1</code> through <code>o-8</code>).","<strong>25 Discrete Overlays Per Bank</strong> (one dedicated overlay for each of the 25 physical keys spanning <strong>C2 to C4</strong> when keyboard Octave is set to <code>0</code>).","<strong><code>o-0</code></strong>: AFX Mode Disabled (Standard base patch active across all keys)."],"ordered":false},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    AFX OVERLAY BANK ALLOCATION MAP                         │\n├───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Bank Register │ Factory Pre-Configuration                                  │\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Bank `o-1`    │ Factory Preset AFX Soundset 1 (Aphex Twin / Artist Presets)│\n│ Bank `o-2`    │ Factory Preset AFX Soundset 2 (Percussive / Drum Kit 1)    │\n│ Bank `o-3`    │ Factory Preset AFX Soundset 3 (Drum Kit 2 / Glitch Hits)   │\n│ Bank `o-4`    │ Factory Preset AFX Soundset 4 (Sound Effects &amp; Modulations)│\n├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Banks `o-5`   │ User Blank Banks (Initialized to match active base patch   │\n│ through `o-8` │ until customized by the user).                             │\n└───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-3","title":"16.1.3: Selecting Overlay Banks","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To enable and select an AFX overlay bank on the hardware:"},{"type":"list","items":["Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong>.","<strong>Press the Arp-Swing key TWICE</strong> (the upper <code>F#</code> key).","The 3-character display indicates the current overlay bank (<code>o-0</code> for Off, or <code>o-1</code> through <code>o-8</code>).","Use the <strong>Patch/Value ▲ and ▼</strong> buttons to select the desired bank.","Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong> to return to play mode."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"2. Hardware Verification & Practical Exercise","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Load Patch <code>0</code>.","Access the Overlay menu (<code>Function</code> + double-tap upper <code>F#</code>); select <code>o-1</code>. Exit Function.","Play chromatic notes up the keyboard from C2 to C4.","Hear each individual key trigger a completely distinct percussion hit, metallic lead, or sound effect."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-4","title":"16.1.4: Editing Key Overlays in Real Time","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Editing an overlay is performed dynamically on the physical hardware:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      REAL-TIME OVERLAY EDITING GESTURE\n   [Hold Desired Key on Keybed] + [Turn Any Front-Panel Control Knob / Fader]\n                                 │\n                                 ▼\n   Only the Held Key's Overlay is Modified (All other 24 keys unaffected!)</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Editing Procedure</strong>:","Ensure an overlay bank (e.g., <code>o-5</code>) is active.","<strong>Press and hold the specific key</strong> you wish to program (e.g., <code>C2</code>).","While holding down the key, adjust any front-panel controls (e.g., change Osc waveform, lower pitch coarse, adjust filter cutoff, increase Overdrive).","Release the key.","Strike adjacent keys (e.g., <code>D2</code>); confirm they retain their original sound while <code>C2</code> plays your newly edited sound."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-5","title":"16.1.5: Committing Bank Writes (Saving AFX Banks)","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"callout","variant":"key","title":"Note","html":"[!IMPORTANT] Modifying key overlays alters data in the volatile overlay buffer. If you change overlay banks or power off the unit without saving, <strong>all overlay edits will be lost</strong>."},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Saving Procedure</strong>:","Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong>, then <strong>double-tap the Arp-Swing key</strong> (upper <code>F#</code>) to enter the overlay bank selection menu (display shows <code>o-1</code>…<code>o-8</code>).","While on the overlay bank menu, press the <strong>Save</strong> button.","The display flashes the active bank number (e.g., <code>o-5</code>).","Press <strong>Save</strong> a second time to commit the entire 25-key bank to non-volatile EEPROM memory."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-6","title":"16.1.6: Copy and Paste Routines Across Key Overlays","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To duplicate a sound from one key to another within an active overlay bank:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">                      OVERLAY COPY / PASTE ROUTINE\n   [Step 1] Hold Source Key (e.g., C2) + Press [Function] + Press [Transpose]\n            ──► Display Flashes `CPY` (Sound Loaded into Copy Buffer)\n   [Step 2] Hold Target Key (e.g., G2) + Press [Function] + Press [Transpose]\n            ──► Display Flashes `PSt` (Sound Pasted onto Target Key!)</pre>"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Copy Gesture</strong>:","Hold down the source key whose sound you want to duplicate.","While holding the key, press <strong>Function</strong> and <strong>Transpose</strong> simultaneously. The display momentarily confirms <strong><code>CPY</code></strong>.","<strong>Paste Gesture</strong>:","Hold down the target key where you want to paste the sound.","While holding the target key, press <strong>Function</strong> and <strong>Transpose</strong> simultaneously. The display confirms <strong><code>PSt</code></strong>."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-7","title":"16.1.7: Overlay Write-Protection","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To prevent accidental modification of your carefully designed AFX drum kits and soundsets during live performances:"},{"type":"list","items":["Press <strong>Function / Exit</strong>.","<strong>Press the SEQ Retrig key TWICE</strong> (the upper <code>G</code> key).","The display indicates <code>r-0</code> (Write-Protect Off) or <code>r-1</code> (Write-Protect On).","When set to <strong><code>r-1</code></strong>, holding keys and turning knobs will <strong>not overwrite overlay memory</strong>."],"ordered":true}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-8","title":"16.1.8: Overlay Parameter Inclusion Matrix","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1. Technical Exposition","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"To prevent timing glitches and operational conflicts, only voice-specific parameters are stored in key overlays:"},{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    OVERLAY PARAMETER INCLUSION MATRIX                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ INCLUDED in Key Overlays            │ EXCLUDED from Overlays (Global Only) │\n├─────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • Oscillator 1 &amp; 2 Waveforms/Pitch  │ • Arpeggiator Settings (Tempo,       │\n│ • Sub-Oscillator Wave &amp; Octave      │   Rhythm, Mode, Octaves, Swing)      │\n│ • Mixer Levels (Osc1/2/Sub/Noise/Ring)│ • Master Tune &amp; Input Gain         │\n│ • Filter Type, Shape, Slope, Cutoff │ • Global MIDI Channel &amp; Local Control│\n│ • Resonance, Overdrive, Tracking    │ • Sequencer 1–4 Memory Patterns      │\n│ • Amp &amp; Mod ADSR Faders             │ • Volume Potentiometer Position      │\n│ • Distortion &amp; Osc Filter Mod       │                                      │\n│ • LFO 1 &amp; 2 Waveforms, Rates, Delays│                                      │\n│ • Aftertouch &amp; Mod Wheel Depths     │                                      │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>"}]}],"minutes":8},{"id":"bassstation-l-16-1-9","title":"16.1.9: Novation Components AFX Management & Autostep Sampling","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"16.1.9: Novation Components AFX Management & Autostep Sampling","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"1. Technical Exposition","level":4},{"type":"prose","html":"Novation Components provides a dedicated graphic AFX editor:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Visual Drum Mapping</strong>: Drag and drop any individual patch from your library directly onto any of the 25 graphical keys.","<strong>Live Edit</strong>: Tweak overlay parameters in real time via the browser or desktop app with full visual feedback.","<strong>Autostep Sampling Helper</strong>:","A specialized sampling utility in Components designed for producers creating sample packs or multisampled instruments.","Automatically steps through each key sequentially with standardized MIDI velocity triggers, allowing external DAWs or hardware samplers to record all 25 analog drum/synth hits into a pristine sample library automatically."],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"Assessment Gate I — Self-Assessment Checkpoint","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Before advancing to Module 17, verify complete mastery of Gate I proficiencies:"},{"type":"list","items":["[ ] <strong>Bank Selection</strong>: Select Overlay Bank <code>o-5</code> using the 2-press Function gesture on the upper <code>F#</code> key.","[ ] <strong>Real-Time Editing</strong>: Build a custom 4-key drum kit (Kick on C2, Snare on D2, Closed Hat on F#2, Open Hat on A#2) by holding each key and turning panel knobs.","[ ] <strong>Copy &amp; Paste</strong>: Execute the <code>Function + Transpose</code> gesture to copy the Closed Hat from F#2 onto G#2, observing <code>CPY</code> and <code>PSt</code> display confirmation.","[ ] <strong>Commit Bank Write</strong>: Commit the modified overlay bank to non-volatile EEPROM memory using the Save routine on the overlay menu.","[ ] <strong>Write-Protect</strong>: Access the <code>r-0/r-1</code> write-protect menu via the upper <code>G</code> key and demonstrate locking the bank against accidental editing."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
